# Broker config -- sourced by cld-broker.sh. Copy to /etc/cld/broker.conf
# (or point CLD_BROKER_CONF at it).
#
# The broker serves ANY repo that has a running master: it resolves the target
# repo from the calling master container's org.cld.repo-root label, and the
# secrets path from that repo's own cld config (pyproject_dir, default .).
# So there is nothing per-repo to configure here -- only broker-wide settings.

RUNTESTS_IMAGE=runtests:latest

# graphql action (docs/impl-graphql-broker-plan.md). GRAPHQL_IMAGE is the
# server image (../graphqlserver/); GRAPHQL_BIND defaults to the docker
# bridge gateway if unset -- same reasoning as sshd's own bridge-only bind,
# see sshd_cld_broker.conf. GRAPHQL_URL_ALLOWLIST is deliberately commented
# out below: empty/unset means no raw http(s):// query targets are allowed at
# all, only "local" and repo-configured aliases -- list hostnames here to
# permit specific ones (space-separated, exact match, no wildcards).
# GRAPHQL_IMAGE=graphqlserver:latest
# GRAPHQL_BIND=172.17.0.1
# GRAPHQL_URL_ALLOWLIST=dev.example.internal staging.example.internal
# GRAPHQL_START_TIMEOUT=300

# The forced command runs with a minimal PATH; make jj, docker, cld (the
# `agent` action runs host-side `cld agent`), curl (the `graphql` action's
# readiness probe and queries), and jq/python3 if your `graphql_command`
# needs them -- plus any other tools your actions call -- reachable:
# PATH=/home/you/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Your ssh-agent socket, forwarded into the agents and task-agents the broker
# launches so they can push their deliverable branch. sshd gives the forced
# command no $SSH_AUTH_SOCK of its own, so without this they run keyless.
# It must be a path that stays valid across logins, because the broker reads it
# per request -- a login-shell agent's /tmp/ssh-XXXX/agent.NNN does not qualify.
# A systemd user unit gives you one:
#     systemctl --user enable --now ssh-agent.service   # with %t/ssh-agent.socket
# SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/run/user/1000/ssh-agent.socket
